<title>SWITZERLAND: SPEED SKATING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SPEED SKATING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>DAVOS, Switzerland 1997-01-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results from a</p>
<p>World Cup speed skating competition on Sunday:</p>
<p>Men's 5,000 metres:</p>
<p>1. Bob de Jong (Netherlands) six minutes, 51.21 seconds</p>
<p>2. Gianni Romme (Netherlands) 6:52.98</p>
<p>3. Frank Dittrich (Germany) 6:54.63</p>
<p>4. Bart Veldkamp (Belgium) 6:56.72</p>
<p>5. Keiji Shirahata (Japan) 6:57.67</p>
<p>6. Rintje Ritsma (Netherlands) 7:02.69</p>
<p>7. KC Boutiette (U.S.) 7:03.38</p>
<p>8. Vadim Sayutin (Russia) 7:04.75</p>
<p>9. Andrei Krivoshjei (Russia) 7:05.02</p>
<p>10. Rene Taubenrauch (Germany) 7:05.26</p>
<p>Women's 1,500m:</p>
<p>1. Gunda Niemann (Germany) 2:03.75</p>
<p>2. Svetlana Bazhanova (Russia) 2:04.24</p>
<p>3. Claudia Pechstein (Germany) 2:04.46</p>
<p>4. Marianne Timmer (Netherlands) 2:05.56</p>
<p>5. Annamarie Thomas (Netherlands) 2:05.68</p>
<p>6. Tonny de Jong (Netherlands) 2:05.77</p>
<p>7. Chiharu Nozaki (Japan) 2:06.30</p>
<p>8. Ulrike Adeberg (Germany) 2:06.45</p>
<p>9. Anette Tonsberg (Norway) 2:06.64</p>
<p>10. Mihaela Dascalu (Romania) 2:07.21</p>
